# AURORA — example environment file
# ===================================================================
# EVERYTHING HERE IS OPTIONAL in the default (bridge) mode. AURORA runs
# perfectly with an empty file — the bridge authenticates off your Claude Code
# login, and voice input and output both fall back to the browser's own speech.
# Copy this to .env.local, and add only what you actually want to change.
#
# The one line worth adding is ELEVENLABS_API_KEY, down in the BRIDGE section:
# it gives you a much better voice and Scribe transcription. The free tier is
# plenty for a demo. Never commit a real key.
#
# Two audiences read these variables:
#   - the BRIDGE (the Node server, bridge/server.mjs) reads the AURORA_*,
#     CAPSULA_* and ELEVENLABS_* variables from .env.local or, taking
#     precedence, from its shell environment.
#   - the FRONTEND (the Vite app) reads the VITE_* variables from .env.local.
# Only VITE_-prefixed values ever reach the browser.


# ===================================================================
# ESTE FORK — português, Windows, memória, REA e Cápsula
# ===================================================================
# Tudo opcional: os padrões abaixo já são os do PC com os discos C:, D: e E:.

# Idioma. Os dois precisam ser iguais (um vale para a ponte, o outro para a
# página). Padrão pt-BR; en-GB fala inglês britânico, como o JARVIS original.
# AURORA_LANG=pt-BR
# VITE_LANG=pt-BR

# Memória em disco. Padrão no Windows: D:\AuroraMemoria, com cópia automática
# em E:\AuroraMemoria (se esses discos existirem); fora do Windows, ~/AuroraMemoria.
# AURORA_MEMORY_BACKUP vazio desliga a cópia; AURORA_MEMORY=off desliga tudo.
# AURORA_MEMORY_DIR=D:\AuroraMemoria
# AURORA_MEMORY_BACKUP=E:\AuroraMemoria
# AURORA_MEMORY=on

# Onde a AURORA salva arquivos grandes (downloads, análises do REA, mídia).
# Padrão no Windows: E:\AuroraArquivos.
# AURORA_FILES_DIR=E:\AuroraArquivos

# Pasta do nó Cápsula, que a AURORA só lê (nunca a carteira nem as chaves).
# Padrão: a pasta .capsula dentro do seu usuário.
# CAPSULA_DIR=C:\Users\voce\.capsula

# O navegador da janela da AURORA (o atalho, o início com o Windows e
# `npm run janela`). Padrão: o Chrome; sem ele, o Edge.
# AURORA_NAVEGADOR=C:\Program Files\Google\Chrome\Application\chrome.exe

# Liberar as ações também quando ela liga sozinha (o mesmo que --writes).
# AURORA_ALLOW_WRITES=1

# Reserva gratuita. Quando o limite do plano do Claude acaba, ela continua num
# modelo que roda neste computador pelo Ollama, avisa uma vez e volta para o
# Claude sozinha quando o limite renova. Prepare uma vez com `npm run ollama`.
#   auto   — o Claude, e o modelo local só enquanto o limite estiver esgotado (padrão)
#   local  — só o modelo local, sem gastar nada do plano
#   claude — só o Claude, sem troca
# AURORA_BRAIN=auto
# Onde o Ollama responde. Padrão http://127.0.0.1:11434.
# AURORA_OLLAMA_URL=http://127.0.0.1:11434
# O modelo que ela usa. Padrão aurora-local, que o `npm run ollama` cria.
# AURORA_OLLAMA_MODEL=aurora-local
# O modelo de base do `npm run ollama` (ou `npm run ollama -- qwen2.5:14b`).
# Padrão qwen2.5:7b com 16 GB de memória ou mais; llama3.2:3b abaixo disso.
# AURORA_OLLAMA_BASE=qwen2.5:7b
# Contexto do aurora-local, em tokens. Padrão 16384.
# AURORA_OLLAMA_CONTEXT=16384
# 1 aceita o uso extra pago do plano antes de trocar. Padrão 0: quando o plano
# acaba ela troca para o modelo local em vez de começar a cobrar extra.
# AURORA_EXTRA_USAGE=0
# Quando o aviso de limite não diz a hora em que ele renova: de quantos em
# quantos minutos tentar o Claude de novo. Padrão 30.
# AURORA_CLAUDE_RETRY_MIN=30

# Guarda de downloads: examina cada programa, instalador, script, APK, arquivo
# compactado ou imagem de disco que chega na pasta Downloads e avisa em voz.
# Só lê; nada é aberto, executado, movido ou apagado. Padrão: a pasta Downloads
# do Windows, mesmo que você a tenha mudado de lugar. "off" desliga a guarda.
# AURORA_DOWNLOADS=C:\Users\voce\Downloads
# Chave da API do VirusTotal (a gratuita serve), para ela dizer quantos
# antivírus já marcaram o arquivo. Só o hash SHA-256 é enviado, nunca o arquivo.
# AURORA_VIRUSTOTAL_KEY=


# ===================================================================
# BRIDGE (the server) — read from the shell that runs `npm run bridge`
# ===================================================================
# These are shown with their defaults. Leave them unset to accept the default.

# Port the bridge listens on (WebSocket + a few HTTP endpoints). Default 8787.
# If you change it, change VITE_BRIDGE_URL to match.
# AURORA_BRIDGE_PORT=8787

# The model the bridge asks Claude Code to run. Default claude-opus-5.
# AURORA_MODEL=claude-opus-5

# Reasoning effort. Default medium.
# AURORA_EFFORT=medium

# Allow effectful tools (send, tap, delete, install, pay). Off by default, so
# AURORA can look at anything and change nothing. `npm start -- --writes` and
# `npm run bridge:writes` turn it on for one run — read the decideTool gate in
# bridge/server.mjs first.
# AURORA_ALLOW_WRITES=0

# Extra browser origins allowed to open the agent WebSocket, comma separated.
# Local dev origins are already allowed; add others only if you serve the app
# from a different address. Default: none.
# AURORA_ALLOWED_ORIGINS=

# Allow clients that send no Origin header at all (curl, scripts, native apps).
# Off by default, because that is also what local malware looks like. Default 0.
# AURORA_ALLOW_NO_ORIGIN=0

# Extra directories the bridge's /file endpoint may serve from, comma separated.
# Your home directory and the system temp directory are always included; this is
# for anything outside them, such as an external drive of footage. Default: none.
# AURORA_FILE_ROOTS=

# ElevenLabs voice id for the bridge's own speech endpoint. Default: Alice,
# a British woman's voice; for Portuguese pick a Brazilian voice in the
# ElevenLabs voice library and paste its id here.
# AURORA_VOICE_ID=Xb7hH8MSUJpSbSDYk0k2

# ElevenLabs API key. Optional. With it, AURORA speaks in the ElevenLabs voice
# and transcribes with ElevenLabs Scribe; without it, everything still works on
# the browser's own speech. If you already have an elevenlabs MCP server in
# ~/.claude.json, the bridge reads the key from there and you can leave this
# blank. Default: none.
# ELEVENLABS_API_KEY=


# ===================================================================
# FRONTEND (Vite) — put these in .env.local
# ===================================================================

# Which brain the browser talks to. Default bridge.
#   bridge — talk to the local bridge (recommended). No API key, and every MCP
#            server in your Claude Code config is available.
#   direct — the browser calls the Claude API itself. Needs VITE_ANTHROPIC_API_KEY.
# VITE_BACKEND=bridge

# Where the bridge listens. Keep the port in step with AURORA_BRIDGE_PORT above.
# Default ws://localhost:8787.
# VITE_BRIDGE_URL=ws://localhost:8787

# Browser text-to-speech engine, used when no ElevenLabs voice is active.
# Default system.
#   system — the browser's built-in speechSynthesis. Instant, on-device.
#   kokoro — a neural voice running in the browser. Better sound, slower to start.
# VITE_TTS_ENGINE=system

# Which Kokoro voice, when VITE_TTS_ENGINE=kokoro. Default bf_emma (British
# woman); bf_isabella, bf_alice and bf_lily too, or the men bm_george and co.
# VITE_KOKORO_VOICE=bf_emma

# Prefer the ElevenLabs voice from the browser when a key is available.
# Default false.
# VITE_USE_ELEVENLABS=false

# Anthropic API key — DIRECT MODE ONLY. Required if and only if
# VITE_BACKEND=direct, and it ships to the browser, so use it only for a local
# demo. The default bridge mode never reads it. Default: none.
# VITE_ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=
